        "original_id": "b6cf8e00-81a2-523c-a30b-a2eabd2d7b7d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, William Rotko, Robert Hanssen, Eric O'Neill, Ryan Phillippe, Tony Giglio, Jason Statham, Wesley Snipes\n- Films: Breach, Chaos, Gosford Park, Crash, Flags of Our Fathers, Stop-Loss\n- Organizations: FBI, Soviet intelligence, Russian intelligence\n- Topics: Espionage, film credits\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Hanssen was born on April 18, 1944.\n- Robert Hanssen was an FBI agent who spied for Soviet and Russian intelligence services against the United States from 1979 to 2001.\n- Chaos is a 2005 thriller film directed by Tony Giglio and starring Jason Statham, Ryan Phillippe, and Wesley Snipes.\n- Breach is a 2007 American historical and political thriller film directed by Billy Ray.\n- The screenplay for Breach was written by Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, and William Rotko.\n- Breach is based on the true story of Robert Hanssen and Eric O'Neill, who helped bring about Hanssen's downfall.\n- Robert Hanssen was convicted of spying for the Soviet Union and later Russia for more than two decades.\n- In the 2000s, Ryan Phillippe appeared in Gosford Park, Crash, Flags of Our Fathers, Breach, and Stop-Loss.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
